SUMMARY:TechTalk (In-Person) - September 2026
DESCRIPTION:Toronto JavaScript\nAfter a brief pause\, we're back with anot
 her in-person event.\n\nHere’s the September edition of our Tech Talk ev
 ent at Super.com on September 29\, 2026\n\nJoin us for some drinks\, snack
 s\, and Tech Talks.\n\nMake sure to mark your calendars\, come out\, and j
 oin us for this event!\n\n**🕑 Agenda & Schedule ✨**\n\n* 18:00 - Door
 s open\n* 18:20 - Intro and announcements\n\n* 18:30 - **httpstate - Synch
 ronizing state across all of your apps** by **[Alex Morales](https://https
 tate.com)**\n*Abstract*: Moving data between frontend\, backend\, apps\, a
 nd databases usually requires complex wiring. httpstate is a lightweight l
 ibrary that handles end-to-end state management in just a few lines of cod
 e—eliminating boilerplate so you can transfer data without the setup ove
 rhead.\n\n* 19:00 - **Strudel - live-coding music in your browser with Jav
 ascript** by **[Fabio Neves](https://fabioneves.ca)**\n*Abstract*: Code is
 n't just for apps—it makes real-time music. While tools like TidalCycles
  and Sonic Pi require external setups\, Strudel is a self-contained JS liv
 e-coding tool running straight in your browser via the Web Audio API. Join
  us as we explore live-coding history and code an EDM track live 🎛️
 🎚️\n\n* 19:30 - Networking\n* 21:00 - Doors Close\n\n(**Note**: *All 
 times in the schedule are an approximation.*)\n\nPlease RSVP to confirm yo
 ur attendance. If you have your friends or teammates joining please ask th
 em to RSVP as well.\n\nThis event is open to all skill levels.\n\nMany tha
 nks to [Super.com](Super.com) for hosting us!\n\nWe're looking for sponsor
 s for events like these. If you or your company would like to support Toro
 ntoJS and get a message out to our community\, please get in touch with or
 ganizers@torontojs.com\n\nThe Code of Conduct is enforced at all TorontoJS
  events and spaces - online or in-person.\n\nTorontoJS is a volunteer-led 
 not-for-profit organization.\n\n**Please help us** with tidying up. Otherw
 ise\, the venue staff and volunteers will have to pick up after you.\n\\-\
 \-\\-\n\n# **The Venue 🏠**\n\nThe venue is next door to Shoppers Drug M
 art\, a nondescript door that you'll have to look for a little carefully.\
 n\\-\\-\\-\n*TorontoJS is committed to creating a safe and inclusive envir
 onment for all. Our Code of Conduct applies both online and in person at a
 ll our events and spaces.*\n\nSee you there! 🎉
